+| Sales-lead admin: list, notes, CSV export and erasure — migration `0009_lead_notes` (`lead_notes`: append-only, `author_id` → users `ON DELETE SET NULL`, cascade on lead delete, non-blank body); the data layer `lead_admin` (every function takes a `VendorAdmin` and a transaction and writes its own audit row; each mutation first locks the lead `FOR UPDATE`, so one racing an erasure is a 404, never a 500) behind six vendor-admin routes whose `VendorAdmin` extractor runs before any path, query or body: `GET /api/admin/leads?segment=&status=&from=&to=` (`segment` one of the four segments or `none` for contact-only leads, `status` `new`\|`contacted`\|`qualified`\|`closed`, `from`/`to` inclusive UTC days `YYYY-MM-DD` matching a lead with **any** submission in the range; empty means any; a bad value 400 with no audit row; latest submission first, then id; at most 100 plus `truncated`; `admin.leads_listed`, subject `search:leads`, `{filter, lead_ids}`), `GET /api/admin/leads/{id}` (`{lead, submissions, notes}`, submissions with their exact consent text and notes with their author, newest first; `admin.lead_viewed` `{}`), `POST /api/admin/leads/{id}/status {status}` (`{lead}`; `admin.lead_status_changed {from, to}` and an `updated_at` bump only on a change), `POST /api/admin/leads/{id}/notes {body}` (201 `{note}`, trimmed, same rules as a lead message; `admin.lead_note_added {note_id}`), `POST /api/admin/leads/{id}/erase` (deletes the lead, its submissions and notes in one transaction; `admin.lead_erased {submissions, notes}`; no suppression record is kept, so the same address submitting again is a new lead), `POST /api/admin/leads/export {segment?, status?, from?, to?}` (a CSRF-protected POST so no other site can start a download; the list's filters and order with no row cap; RFC 4180 `text/csv; charset=utf-8`, `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="sales-leads-<UTC date>.csv"`, `Cache-Control: no-store`; cells starting `=`, `+`, `-`, `@`, TAB or CR prefixed with `'`